id: pm-vcs-l8jv
title: Documented TOON record paths fail staging because the record codec accepts JSON only
description: "The README's primary init example configures .agents/pm/**/*.toon as first-class records, but staging a real pm-initialized tracker calls the JSON-only record decoder and aborts with record payload is not valid JSON. This prevents pm-vcs from using pm's native item format as the structured merge primitive it advertises."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: "format:toon",pm-sdk,real-data,records
created_at: "2026-08-01T03:59:00.345Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T03:59:00.345Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: A real installed-CLI test stages native TOON item and history data through the registered extension; canonical TOON decoding and encoding preserve all supported pm fields; per-field merge handles concurrent PM item edits; JSON record paths remain compatible; README examples are executable.
parent: pm-vcs-tr2a
severity: high
repro_steps: Initialize a fresh pm workspace; install pm-vcs; run pm vcs init with record path .agents/pm/**/*.toon; create a Task with pm; run pm vcs add.
expected_result: Native PM TOON items stage as record objects and later merge per field without losing TOON semantics or history.
actual_result: pm vcs add aborts with Record payload is not valid JSON.
affected_version: 2026.7.30
component: engine/records
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  engine/model.ts,project,record codec boundary
  README.md,project,documented TOON example
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "npm run release:check",project,2400
body: ""
